 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? There are few family friendly ones like Story Train Series and Stick Man. Have you tried those? Then animal podcasts are great. The ear loom is one where a kid reads them and they're all about different creatures. They' all age appropriate narratives, with little pop ups that explain big words. The author even reads them out. Best done together, really. Lots of podcasts are structured like stories, so they're easy to follow. I' sure she will. Many young listeners start off just listening along with a parent, and then they move on on their own.",
